{
  "rationale": "The plant separates perception (obstacle events) from motion commands, modeling the robot's open-loop motion and sensor-driven state. The specification enforces safe, progress-oriented exploration: forward/random_walk in clear, rotate_clockwise for left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right, move_backward for front, and full_rotate only as a last-resort after repeated blockages. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state. Recovery states are one-shot and return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model robot's perception and motion as a single plant automaton with helper states for committed actions and recovery.",
